  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations, lightheadedness, and intermittent syncope suggestive of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation (I49.5) and sick sinus syndrome (I48.0). Given the personal history of transient ischemic attack and cerebral infarction, continuous mobile cardiac telemetry monitoring (CPT 93229) is ordered to detect arrhythmic events and guide appropriate anticoagulation and rate-control management. This service is medically necessary to evaluate the documented arrhythmias and prevent recurrent ischemic events in a patient with a history of cerebrovascular disease."
